	<key>readme</key>
	<string>A calculator you type at in plain words, in an Alfred UI window. Needs Alfred 6 and calculingo for Mac (free, calculingo.app/features), which gives the answers and starts by itself, out of sight.

  calc                          the window
  calc from 1 jan to christmas  the window, already answering

Dates and the gap between them, the time in another city, money at today's rate, units, the sun and the moon, and maths from a sum to a percentile. The answer updates on every keystroke.

Eight answers copied or pasted a day are free. A calculingo Pro license in the app makes them unlimited: store.calculingo.app.

Nothing in the list is chosen until you press ↓. A row only ever fills the line; the answer is copied from the line. The keys along the bottom say what they will do.

↩ fills the line from the chosen row, or copies the line's answer and closes (finishing a half-typed line first); ⌘↩ pastes it into the app you were in; ⌘⇧C copies and stays open. ⇥ fills the line with whatever is on offer (the chosen row, the example in an empty box, the rest of a word) to keep typing. → does the same while a row is chosen or the box shows its example. ↓/↑ (⌃N/⌃P, ⌃J/⌃K) move through the list, and ↑ from the first row goes back to the line. ⌘1–⌘9 fill the line from that row. ⌘⇧⌫ forgets the chosen recent question. ⌘O (or Open in Browser) asks the question on calculingo.app. ⌘⌫ (or Clear History) forgets every recent question, with Undo. esc steps back: the list, then the line, then the window.

https://calculingo.app</string>
